1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Thank you, Killua.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
I owe it all to you.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
It was like that ever since I woke up.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
It was you, Killua.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
If it means helping Gon,

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
I'm ready to do anything in my power.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
But please don't forget,

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
out of all the people
Gon needs in his life,

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
he needs you the most.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[gasping]

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[opening theme music playing]

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
[singer singing in English]

15
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
to ignore Meleoron's heartfelt protests

16
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
and appeared before them in the room

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
to force a confrontation with Pouf.

18
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
[Knuckle] Pouf.

19
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[sighs]

20
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
The body that stands before you
is merely a shell.

21
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
My true core is on its way
to the King as we speak.

22
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[sighs]

23
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
[gasps]

24
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[intense music playing]

25
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[narrator] Having recently
escaped from the cage of smoke,

26
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Pouf confirmed that Knuckle and Morel

27
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,000
had indeed made contact
exactly as he suspected.

28
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
This was the right call.

29
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
The boss already told me

30
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
that you could make segments.
You're not lying.

31
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
[narrator] It was solely for Gon's benefit

32
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Hang on.

33
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Why are you telling me all this, anyway?

34
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
and had chosen not to share
this information with Pouf.

35
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[Shaiapouf] Depending on his reason…

36
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Answer me, damn it!

37
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[Shaiapouf] My aim was to satisfy him.

38
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
[gasps]

39
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
and, for that, he needed
to leave the room peacefully.

40
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
I thought it might
put the boy's mind at ease.

41
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
He made it perfectly clear

42
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
that I was not to leave
this room for any reason.

43
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
I am only a segment

44
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
but what I seek is
a discussion and nothing more.

45
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
That is why I revealed the truth.

46
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[narrator] Pouf knew
that when dealing with opponents

47
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
who would call him from behind
to challenge him,

48
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
appearing to tell the truth

49
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
would be far more effective
than relying on deception.

50
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
[Gon] You're lying.

51
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
[Shaiapouf gasps]

52
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[Gon] Earlier…

53
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
you tried to sneak up
from behind and kill me.

54
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
You even admitted it.

55
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Knuckle, don't let him fool you.

56
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Is there any way that you can prove it?

57
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[grunts]

58
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
[Knuckle] He's right.

59
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
[violin music playing]

60
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Out of all of our enemies,

61
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
I dare say that he possesses
the strongest will of all.

62
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
But now, he's preoccupied with Pitou.

63
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Perhaps I should be pleased by this.

64
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
It may yet work in our favor.

65
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
It's because of his iron will
and his incredible focus

66
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
that he's sitting there.

67
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
I would be putting myself
at a disadvantage,

68
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
so I can say nothing.

69
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
I'm afraid you will have to use
your own judgment.

70
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Think it over.

71
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Whether you come or not
is up to you!

72
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
[groans]

73
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
[Neferpitou] Please wait!

74
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Look! I'm still right here!

75
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
I am so sorry about Pouf.

76
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I'm the only one you need, right?

77
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
[Gon] Ten minutes.

78
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[gasps]

79
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
You're just gonna have
to heal her ten minutes faster.

80
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:15,000
ignored Pouf's provocation
and slashed Pitou's deadline.

81
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
For how long?
How long should we wait?

82
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:43,000
and I can heal
her most critical injuries.

83
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[narrator] Originally, Pitou had asked

84
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
for a greater amount of time
than was necessary.

85
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
This was to protect Komugi

86
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
and allow time for her
to heal completely.

87
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Gon did not comply.

88
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
After a brief negotiation,
they agreed on one hour,

89
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:10,000
However, as a direct result
of experience,

90
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Perhaps it was coincidence,

91
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
but it was likely that Gon
had only chosen ten minutes

92
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,000
to conform with Pouf's parting words.

93
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Despite that probability,

94
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
because if I don't…

95
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[roars]

96
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
I understand.

97
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
[Knuckle] Hmm.

98
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[Gon] Knuckle…

99
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
I'll be fine here by myself.

100
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
his true core is headed for the King…

101
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
and the King is to the south.

102
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,000
[dramatic music playing]

103
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[narrator] Gon and Killua
had seen everything

104
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
that had transpired up to this point,

105
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:32,000
but since Pitou
had no way of knowing this,

106
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
it was only natural to assume that Gon

107
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:39,000
had seen through Pouf's scheme
and already knew his plans.

108
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Neferpitou] I have to kill him,
no matter the cost.

109
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I must, for the King's sake.

110
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
First, I must entrust her to someone else.

111
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
If I'm gone,

112
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
who will take Komugi to the King?

113
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Gon, I can tell what you want to say,
believe me,

114
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
but it doesn't matter,

115
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
because I'm still gonna do things my way.

116
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Youpi was…

117
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[gasps]

118
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
No. No, never mind.

119
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[narrator] Suddenly,
Knuckle realized that if what he said

120
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
made Gon hesitate even for a moment,

121
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
it could quite easily result in his death.

122
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
See ya.

123
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
[narrator] At the last second,
Knuckle managed to stop himself.

124
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
[Netero] Simple, really.

125
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:54,000
My subordinates were present
at your mother's deathbed.

126
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
She uttered your name
with her dying breath.

127
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
I bet I'm the only one who knows now.

128
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Those same subordinates probably
died fighting your Royal Guard.

129
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
[wind blowing]

130
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
I'll make you a deal.

131
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
If you can force me to admit defeat,

132
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
I'll tell you your name.

133
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
[scoffs]

134
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
So I'll be playing
without a rook and bishop.

135
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
[Netero] When?

136
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
When did I start waiting

137
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,000
for my opponent
to make the first move?

138
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[scoffs]

139
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
[yells]

140
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Hah!

141
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,000
[thump]

142
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
[blow cracks]

143
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
[yells]

144
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[man 1] Hah!

145
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
[thump]

146
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[blow cracks]

147
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[man 2] Yah!

148
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
When did I stop hesitating
and start graciously accepting

149
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
as they bowed their heads in defeat?

150
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
As if that was what I wanted!

151
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:17,000
That's not the height of perfection
that I sought for so long!

152
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[boom]

153
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
I have always dreamt
of giving my heart and soul

154
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
to battle an unstoppable adversary.

155
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[chorus vocalizing]

156
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
[Netero] This is a tomb.

157
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Yours, as a matter of fact.

158
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[chorus continues]

159
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[rumbling]

160
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,000
[chorus ends]

161
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Grateful for everything
that's led me to this point,

162
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
and to you.

163
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
[closing theme music playing]

164
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[upbeat music playing]

165
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Gon] Next time, "Zero and Rose."

166
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Killua] Yeah.

167
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon and Killua] The future is ours.

168
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
